Show the storm window and what the hail sources actually are

The list could not answer "what happened this year". A rolling month count
has no way to express it, so windows are now explicit and resolve to real
dates that the engine, the tests and the screen all share.

Storm coverage is reported source by source. MRMS/MESH radar hail is named
as not configured rather than blended into one count that reads as complete
- it needs server-side GRIB2 processing, which a browser cannot do.

The qualifying storms are carried on the run so the count can be checked
against the events behind it.

